    "result": "Let me verify the fix works one final time by showing the key changes:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. Here's what I did:\n\n### Root Cause\nThe `gate` command in frai-cli was using `[args...]` with commander.js, which only captures positional arguments, not options like `--ci`. The `--ci` flag was being lost before reaching the frai-gate CLI.\n\n### The Fix\nIn `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`, I modified the gate command (lines 737-757):\n\n**Before:**\n- Command definition: `.command('gate [args...]')`\n- Action received `args` parameter from commander\n- Only positional arguments were passed through\n\n**After:**\n- Command definition: `.command('gate')` (no variadic args)\n- Extract all arguments after 'gate' directly from `process.argv`\n- Pass complete args array including options to frai-gate CLI\n\nThis ensures all flags like `--ci` are properly forwarded to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n### Tests\nI created comprehensive tests in `src/gate.test.ts` that verify:\n1. \u2705 `frai gate init --ci` creates both FRAI-SPEC.md and .github/workflows/rai-gate.yml\n2. \u2705 `frai gate init` (without --ci) creates only FRAI-SPEC.md\n\nBoth tests pass successfully.\n\nThe fix is now ready and working correctly. You can commit it with:\n```bash\ngit add packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts packages/frai-cli/src/gate.test.ts\ngit commit -m \"Fix: pass through --ci flag in frai gate command\"\n```",
